From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vincenzopio <43883474+vincenzopio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 01:38:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] service: sign in on the launcher channel.

LAUNCHER_SIGN_IN carries what Microsoft's sign-in page posted, its ServerData. The service
registers the device if it is not registered yet, exchanges the page's token for the account's
tokens as xodus-cli login does, and keeps them in its Keychain service with the user. SignInResult
says that the user is signed in, that Microsoft wants the user on another page first
(inline_auth_url, whose data comes in a second SIGN_IN), or why the sign-in failed.

The keychain is now opened before the channel is served, and a panic in the channel's task stops
the service, as closing the channel does.

Original work for macrock (GPL-3.0-only, as Xodus).

Topic: account
